Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Updated Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report  MS 09  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  CASE  MS 09  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  Date Taken  REMOVED_DATE Source Care Unit  Surg General  WAC 460 MEEI MRN  REMOVED_DATE Path Subspecialty Service  Breast 1 Results To  CHARLES M FERGUSON  M D  Resident  Olga Kolman  M D  Signed Out by  Ronald Balassanian  M D             Addended Report             Reason for Addendum  1  Additional Immunohistochemistry Results Reason for Addendum  2  Additional Fluorescence In Situ Hybridization  FISH  Results CLINICAL DATA  The patient is a 91 year old woman with a palpable lump in the left breast at 2 00 o clock  FINAL DIAGNOSIS  BREAST  LEFT   CORE BIOPSY  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE REMOVED_DATE SEE NOTE  NOTE  Sections of the core biopsy reveal an invasive carcinoma spanning a distance of at least 0 8cm  The tumor grows in large nests and trabeculae of malignant epithelial cells with a prominent dense lymphoid infiltrate present  The tumor cells are large and markedly pleomorphic with ill defined cytoplasm and have enlarged hyperchromatic nuclei with vesicular chromatin and prominent nucleoli  The morphologic findings are compatible with high grade invasive ductal carcinoma  The results of immunohistochemical staining for estrogen receptor  progesterone receptor  and Her2 neu protein expression and of fluorescence in situ hybridization studies for Her2 neu gene amplification will be reported in an addendum  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN and  left breast  are 6 cylindrical gray white to yellow fibrofatty soft tissue cores ranging from REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm to REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm  The specimen is submitted in toto as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Final Diagnosis by Ronald Balassanian M D   Electronically signed on Thursday REMOVED_MONTH 19   REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 03 27 59PM By his her signature above  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  ADDENDUM NOTE  REASON   1 QUANTITATIVE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  Focally  the tumor cells show moderate  2   overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2  See note  Note  Estrogen and progesterone receptor quantitation  The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the tumor cells is assessed visually and reported as follows  The tumor cells stain    10  of nuclei stained  Some tumor cells stain  1 to  10  of nuclei stained  Rare tumor cells stain    1  of nuclei stained  The tumor cells do not stain  0  of nuclei stained  HER 2 c erbB 2 quantitation  the tumor cells membrane immunoreactivity is evaluated visually and reported as follows  Do not show overexpression  0 to 1   no minimal immunoreactivity or incomplete membrane staining of tumor cells  Show moderate  2   overexpression  weak to moderate complete membrane immunoreactivity in   10  of tumor cells  Show strong  3   overexpression  strong complete membrane immunoreactivity in   10  of tumor cells  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Addendum  1 by Atul K Bhan M D   Electronically signed on Monday REMOVED_MONTH 23   REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 08 52 31AM By his her signature above  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  ADDENDUM NOTE  REASON   2 RESULTS OF FLUORESCEN