Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report  MS 08  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  CASE  MS 08  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  Date Taken  REMOVED_DATE Source Care Unit  RAD Mammography Path Subspecialty Service  Breast 1 Results To  KEVIN S  HUGHES  M D  RACHEL ANN HITT  M D  CONNIE ROCHE  NP Resident  Russell Ryan  M D  Signed Out by  Ronald Balassanian  M D  CLINICAL DATA  The patient is a 59 year old woman with two left breast mass lesions  Lesion  1  specimen  A   is a BIRADS 5 on mammogram and U S and is located at 4 00 o clock  Lesion  2  specimen  B   is a 3 to 4cm heterogeneous mass on U S at 1 o clock  possibly a fibroadenoma  located at 1 00 o clock  FINAL DIAGNOSIS  BREAST  LEFT  4 00   CORE BIOPSY  1  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  see note   NOTE  The tumor is composed of large cells with abundant cytoplasm and fairly low nuclear to cytoplasmic ratio  The nuclei have irregular contours and hyperchromatic vesicular chromatin with prominent nucleoli  To confirm the diagnosis  we performed a panel of immunostains with the following results  STAIN TARGET RESULT E cadherin Ductal differentiation Positive Cytokeratin Epithelial cells Positive  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Epithelial subset Positive  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Epithelial subset Positive CDX 2 GI epithelium Negative  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Macrophages Negative TTF 1 Lung Thyroid Negative Vimentin Renal cell CA Negative The immunoperoxidase staining pattern supports the morphologic findings and overall  the findings are compatible with invasive ductal carcinoma  BREAST  LEFT  1 00   CORE BIOPSY  2  BENIGN BREAST PARENCHYMA WITH HYALINIZED STROMA  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  see note   NOTE  The findings may not correlate with the clinical impression of a mass lesion  Clinical correlation to ensure adequate sampling of the targeted lesion is suggested  Multiple levels were examined  By his her signature below  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received are two containers  which are all  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN  Received in formalin  labeled  left breast  1 of 2  4 o clock   are three cores of fibrofatty tissue ranging from REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm to REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm which are submitted in toto as cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received in formalin  labeled  breast 1 o clock  2 of 2   are three cores of fibrofatty tissue ranging from REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm to REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm which are submitted in toto as cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Final Diagnosis by Ronald Balassanian M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE PART A  BREAST  LEFT  4 00   CORE BIOPSY  1 PART B  BREAST  LEFT  4 00   CORE BIOPSY  2  report_end  , Unknown.
